Change(genesis='66602cd0dec37d58d03eec9518ca805a7ac38ea912d2b0c366a0b67b4b9f50b6', deps=(), event=Decided(decision='secretaryproposes', at=datetime(2026, 9, 9, 0, 0, 0), actor='assistant', title='The secretary proposes and the owner taps; only POST proposals/<n>/tap turns a proposal into mail', body="*The secretary proposes and the owner taps* (2026-09-09, ARCHITECTURE §10.3). The `Secretary` record carries no sending effect; `propose_email` STORES a whole message (account, recipients, subject, body) in the conversation, shown in the app with every field. Only `POST …/proposals/<n>/tap` turns one into mail, and its handler needs a `suzatary_core::secretary::tap::Tap`, whose one constructor `Tap::of` takes a `signatures::Trusted`, the door's proof that a device key the history trusts for the actor a named tailnet peer maps to signed the request, plus the CSRF triple. That covers what the record cannot: a ROUTE holds more than its record and could otherwise reach the transport crate. Loopback mints no `Tap`, so the box's shell and the triage agent are refused. The TAP CARRIES AN INDEX, NEVER A BODY: what is sent is what was stored and shown. Exactly ONE file names the transport (`app/cli/tests/writes.rs` pins it): `commands::mail::deliver`, which the human's `send` calls and the tap reaches through its postman.", rationale='Decided 2026-09-09 (ARCHITECTURE §10.3).', supersedes=()))